cdk: don't forget the grab cursor on keyboard ungrabs

The XI2 ungrab clears the remembered grab cursor unconditionally, but
the device being ungrabbed can be a keyboard: releasing a keyboard grab
while the pointer grab of the device pair is still active erases the
image the pointer grab remembered, and the unpin request sent with the
first pointer movement finds a None remembered cursor and returns
early, so the frozen image keeps following the pointer over the whole
screen until the grab ends instead of swapping to the theme's default
arrow.

Only clear the remembered cursor when the device being ungrabbed is not
a keyboard, like the core backend does on its pointer ungrabs and like
the XI2 grab does when it remembers the cursor only on non-keyboard
devices.
